// Guardrails in Policy at the Gateway (AgentCore, June 17, 2026). Chapter 4, Section 4.5.
// Gate 3 with a language check: deny support___create_ticket when the
// Guardrails prompt-attack score on the ticket body exceeds 0.4 (AgentCore's
// suggested default for prompt attack). Scores arrive in steps of 0.2.
// Detection is probabilistic; the decision is deterministic.
//
// A forbid whose only gate is a guardrail looks unconditional to policy
// validation and is reported "Overly Restrictive" unless a permit for the same
// action exists. Create the permit first, or submit with IGNORE_ALL_FINDINGS.
// The Gateway execution role needs bedrock:InvokeGuardrailChecks.
// Untested by the author.

forbid (
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"support___create_ticket",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:REGION:ACCOUNT:gateway/GATEWAY_ID"
)
when guardrails {
  BedrockGuardrails::PromptAttack(["PROMPT_INJECTION"], [context.input.title])["PROMPT_INJECTION"]
    .confidenceScore.greaterThan(decimal("0.4"))
};
